            <ArticleTitle>Pancreatic torsion in a dog.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>476-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 6-month-old male intact Cane Corso mastiff dog was presented for a recent history of vomiting, abdominal pain, and lethargy. A diagnosis of pancreatic torsion was made during abdominal exploratory surgery and was confirmed with histopathology. The dog underwent partial pancreatectomy and recovered with no complications.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
